stems","location":"Chennai","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4461908822","experience":"Lead","skills":[1,14,15,16,17,18,19,20,25,29,34],"is_walkin":false,"linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4461908822","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4461908822"},{"title":"Applied Scientist, CMT","company":"Amazon","location":"Chennai","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4464372512","skills":[1,2,12,25,26,101,112],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**Description**\n As a member of the CMT team, you'll play a key role in the evolution of our Competitive Monitoring systems to solve significantly complex and interesting technical challenges in machine learning, large language models in production, and recommender systems to name a few. The team's work directly impacts customer experience at a worldwide scale.\n   \n\n  \n\n Key job responsibilities\n   \n\n  \n\n* Research the problem domain and come up with various approaches to solve the problem.\n* Be willing to experiment quickly and fail fast.\n* Collaborate with engineers to come up with the right end to end solution to the business problems.\n* Ideate on future roadmap for science in CMT\n* Be willing to roll up your sleeves and learn core topics outside applied science, for example ML engineering\n\n\n A day in the life\n   \n\n  \n\n A typical day might involve (a) working on ideas for improving models around product similarity or price recommendations, (b) working closely with other scientists and our ML engineers to ensure that the best models are in production, (c) writing good maintainable code that can be reused and reproduced, (d) sharing your work across CMT and beyond via technical writings and presentations\n   \n\n  \n\n**Basic Qualifications**\n* Experience programming in Java, C\\+\\+, Python or related language\n* Experience with SQL and an RDBMS (e.g., Oracle) or Data Warehouse\n* Experience building machine learning models or developing algorithms for business application\n* Experience in state\\-of\\-the\\-art deep learning models architecture design and deep learning training and optimization and model pruning\n\n\n**Preferred Qualifications**\n* Experience implementing algorithms using both toolkits and self\\-developed code\n* Have publications at top\\-tier peer\\-reviewed conferences or journals\n\n\n Our inclusive culture empowers Amazonians to deliver the best results for our customers. If you have a disability and need a workplace accommodation or adjustment during the application and hiring process, including support for the interview or onboarding process, please visit https://amazon.jobs/content/en/how\\-we\\-hire/accommodations for more information. If the country/region you\u2019re applying in isn\u2019t listed, please contact your Recruiting Partner.\n   \n\n  \n\n  \n\n**Company** \n \\- ADCI \\- Tamil Nadu\n   \n\n  \n\n Job ID: A10530901","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4464372512","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4464372512"},{"title":"AI/ML Engineer","company":"Saaki Argus and Averil Consulting","location":"Chennai","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4465041444","experience":"10 Yrs","skills":[1,14,15,16,17,18,19,20,25,26,30],"is_walkin":false,"description":"Job Title: AI/ML Engineer\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Experience: 5 \u2013 10 Years\n \n\n\n\n Location: Chennai \u2013 Work from Office, 5 Days a Week\n \n\n\n\n Shift: General Shift\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Key Skills: Python, TensorFlow, Generative AI, Machine Learning, AWS, FastAPI (Mandatory)\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n We are looking for a Gen AI / Machine Learning Engineer with strong experience in Python, TensorFlow, Generative AI, Machine Learning, AWS, and FastAPI.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n The candidate should have experience in building and deploying production\\-grade ML models and pipelines, along with a good understanding of the ML lifecycle and MLOps. Hands\\-on experience with tools such as MLflow, Kubeflow, AWS SageMaker, Vertex AI, Weights \\& Biases, DVC, Airflow, or Prefect is preferred.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Experience with Git, Docker, Jenkins, Kubernetes, Kafka, and CI/CD pipelines is required. Knowledge of AWS, GCP, or Azure and cloud deployment and orchestration tools is expected. Experience with third\\-party integrations is a plus.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n The candidate should be proficient in Python and ML frameworks such as TensorFlow, Keras, or PyTorch, with experience in statistical modeling, machine learning, data mining, unstructured data analytics, and data engineering pipelines.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n The role requires someone who can work independently and collaboratively with multi\\-functional teams, principals, and architects across different geographies, while being comfortable with both hands\\-on technical implementation and high\\-level architecture.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4465041444","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4465041444"},{"title":"Machine Learning(8+yrs Senior Technical Lead)","company":"Veltris","location":"Chennai","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4464981987","experience":"Lead","skills":[1,25,27,28,112],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**Core Focus Areas:** \n\n\n\n* Agentic Automation: Multi\\-agent orchestration platforms for manufacturing and business process automation\n* Enterprise LLM Integration: RAG pipelines, knowledge bases, and domain\\-specific fine\\-tuning\n* Manufacturing Automation: Computer vision pipelines, quality control, process monitoring, assembly line digitalization\n* Internal Business Automation: Finance, HR, Compliance, Operations workflow optimization\n* AI Governance: Establishing frameworks, model evaluation, prompt management at enterprise scale\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Experience Requirements:** \n\n\n\n* 8\\+ years in AI/ML with 5\\+ years in LLMs and generative AI\n* Demonstrated multi\\-agent system deployment experience\n* Strong Python proficiency and ML framework expertise\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Nice\\-to\\-Have Skills:** \n\n\n\n* Computer vision (YOLO, transformers, multimodal LLMs)\n* Manufacturing/Industry 4\\.0 domain knowledge\n* Agentic frameworks (LangGraph, CrewAI, LangChain)\n* Vector databases, MLOps tools\n* AI governance and functional safety standards","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4464981987","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4464981987"}]